.TH OPENFORTIGUI 1 "2026-07-30" "openfortiGUI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openfortigui \- Qt GUI for openfortivpn, a Fortinet SSL-VPN client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openfortigui
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B openfortigui
.B \-\-start\-vpn
.B \-\-vpn\-name
.I name
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openfortiGUI
manages several Fortinet SSL-VPN connections and groups of connections.
openfortivpn is built in, so no separate client is needed.
.PP
Without arguments the graphical interface starts. It runs as the ordinary user
and starts the privileged part of each connection as a separate process through
.BR sudo (8),
using the rule in
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/openfortigui .
The two processes talk over a unix socket whose path the interface passes to the
child; nothing is inherited through the environment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-start\-vpn
Run as the privileged VPN process instead of starting the interface. Requires
root and
.BR \-\-vpn\-name .
This is what the interface invokes; there is rarely a reason to call it by hand.
.TP
.BI \-\-vpn\-name " name"
Name of the profile to connect, as shown in the interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-main\-config " path"
Use
.I path
instead of
.IR ~/.openfortigui/main.conf .
Profiles, logs and the certificate cache follow it, so a second configuration is
fully separate from the default one. The file has to exist; a path that does not
is ignored.
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-socket " path"
Path of the unix socket between the interface and the VPN processes. Defaults to
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/openfortiGUI
and is passed on to every child process.
.TP
.B \-\-kill\-vpn\-processes
Terminate all running VPN processes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.openfortigui/main.conf
Settings of the interface.
.TP
.I ~/.openfortigui/vpnprofiles/
One file per connection profile.
.TP
.I ~/.openfortigui/vpngroups/
One file per group of connections.
.TP
.I ~/.openfortigui/logs/
Log of the interface and one log per connection.
.TP
.I /etc/openfortigui/vpnprofiles/
System-wide profiles, available to every user.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/openfortigui
Permits members of group
.B sudo
to start the VPN process as root. Without it, or without membership in that
group, connecting fails with a request for a password that the interface cannot
answer.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the api socket is created when
.B \-\-api\-socket
is not given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openfortivpn (1),
.BR sudoers (5)
.PP
Documentation and issue tracker:
.UR https://github.com/theinvisible/openfortigui
